          {
            title: 'Tute gana-pierde',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Tute gana-pierde: win-lose Tute variant. First to reach target wins; or lose condition. 40-card Spanish.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Tute originated in Italy as tutti and spread to Spain in the 19th century, becoming one of the most popular card games there. Tute gana-pierde is a Spanish variant in which the player with the most points loses unless someone reaches 101 or more to win; it is played by three to five players individually.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Three to five players.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard Spanish 40-card pack (four suits: Oros, Copas, Espadas, Bastos; ranks 2–7 plus Sota, Caballo, Rey, As).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cards',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'All cards dealt one at a time anticlockwise; last card exposed for trump.',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
